  "goodToKnow": "Anpacken means to tackle a task or problem (Packen wir's an! Let's get to it) and to lend a hand: mit anpacken. It suggests a hands-on, practical attitude, and politicians like to present themselves as Anpacker. Literally, it means to grab: jemanden hart anpacken (to treat someone roughly). Packen also means to manage: Das packst du! (you can do it!). Separable: packte an, angepackt."
